WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.380
In 1654, the French thinker Blaise
Pascal wrote a short private note,

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.660
which he called his Memorial.

3
00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:13.500
In it he set the God of Abraham, Isaac and
Jacob against the God of the philosophers.

4
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:18.290
Is the God that believers trust the
same God that philosophers argue for?

5
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.150
So can Christians reason their way to God?

6
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.460
Or must faith come first?

7
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:27.180
In this mission, you'll test
Christian beliefs through four lenses,

8
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:31.570
starting with: are they
reasonable, meaningful, coherent?

9
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.020
Then you'll see how philosophy
has changed Christian doctrine,

10
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.770
not only defended it.

11
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.890
Your mission: weigh up whether
Christians can reason their way to God,

12
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.920
or whether faith must come first.
